From: build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 0016] no silent defaults on the carry path

Found by running the wiring instead of trusting it:

    python3 -c "print(config.load({}).MAX_NOTIONAL_USD)"
    AttributeError: 'Config' object has no attribute 'MAX_NOTIONAL_USD'

THREE DEFECTS, ALL IN 0015, ALL INVISIBLE

1. getattr(cfg, "MAX_NOTIONAL_USD", 100.0)
   The key does not exist in Config. The carry book's risk cap was INVENTED by
   a default that happened to be right, and was NOT connected to
   shadow.SHADOW_MAX_NOTIONAL_USD - the constant promotion_gate re-derives its
   cap check from. Move the real cap and the gate would police a number the
   book does not use. A risk parameter with a silent default is not a risk
   parameter.

2. hasattr(store, "next_order_sequence")
   Wrong name; the real method is next_order_seq. The guard swallowed it and
   returned 0 forever. Consequence: the same intent on a later candle rebuilds
   the SAME orderLinkId, the venue rejects it as a duplicate, and CarryBroker
   correctly resolves duplicates by QUERYING THE ID - returning the OLD fill.
   The book would believe it had re-opened a position it never placed.

3. store.engage_kill_switch(...)
   Wrong name; the real method is trip_kill_switch. The lambda raised,
   CarryEngine caught it and logged "kill switch itself failed", the book
   halted IN MEMORY, and the PERSISTED switch was never set. A restart would
   resume trading.

Each was hidden by a default or a guard. All three now call the real names
directly. An AttributeError at construction is the correct outcome for a
misnamed dependency.

THE LINE THIS PATCH DRAWS
BOOK_MODE keeps a default; the cap does not. Deliberate, not inconsistent:
  a MODE SELECTOR absent means nobody asked for the carry book, and the legacy
  path is the conservative reading (and dozens of test doubles pass minimal
  config stubs).
  a RISK LIMIT absent means nobody set the limit, and inventing one is how a
  $100 cap silently becomes whatever literal is in the source.
An unrecognised BOOK_MODE now RAISES: a typo must not select a strategy.

 + tests/test_carry_wiring_authority.py   14 tests, including one that patches
   shadow.SHADOW_MAX_NOTIONAL_USD to 250 and asserts the book follows - proving
   the cap and the gate are JOINED, not merely equal today. Others assert the
   real StateStore actually has next_order_seq and trip_kill_switch, that the
   sequence advances so link ids differ, that the halt reaches the PERSISTED
   switch, and that no hasattr guard exists anywhere in the carry wiring.

 ~ tests/test_carry_wiring.py   the stub store used the WRONG method names, so
   it passed while production would have failed at its first order. A test
   double kinder than reality tests nothing.

VERIFIED: 5,162 passed, 2 skipped (was 5,148). Fixture md5 stable. No test
weakened or skipped.

